# Changelog

All notable changes to the Marine Eco System  website are recorded here.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/), and the project uses semantic version numbers.

## [Unreleased]

### Changed

- Moved the navigation bar to the top of every page so that all branding and page content appears below it.

### Planned

- Replace placeholder business contact details with confirmed information.
- Connect forms to a secure server-side form service when backend development is allowed.
- Add CSS styling during the styling phase of the project.

## [1.0.0] - 2026-07-28

### Added

- *2026-07-28:** Created five complete HTML5 pages: Home, About, Services, Inquiry and Contact.
- **2026-08-06:** Consistent navigation and footer across all pages.
- **2026-08-06:** Implemented Semantic page structure and accessibility labels.
- **2026-07-28:** Responsive viewport metadata for mobile browsers.
- **2026-07-28:** Included search-engine descriptions and unique page titles.
- **2026-07-28:** Written service descriptions for the physical cleanups drives, dedicated wildlife rehabilitation and protection.
- **2026-08-11:** Designed Inquiry, quotation and service-booking request form with HTML validation.
- **2026-08-13:** Contact form with HTML validation.
- **2026-08-13:** Added a Business operating-hours table.
- **2026-08-13:** Created README with setup, testing, publishing and version-control guidance.

---


## [1.0.0] - 2026-09-17

### Added
- Initial release of the Marine Eco System website
- **Home Page** (`index.html`) with project overview and featured marine initiatives
- **About Page** with History, Mission Statement, and Vision Statement
- **Services Page** showcasing:
  - Coastal & Beach Cleanups
  - Wildlife Rehabilitation Support
  - Community Education & Outreach
- **Enquiry Page** with detailed form for:
  - Volunteer Sign-up
  - General Enquiries
  - Donations & Sponsorships
  - Guided Marine Tours
- **Contact Us Page** including:
  - Postal and physical address
  - Opening hours
  - Google Maps embed (Summerstrand, Gqeberha)
  - Contact form
- Shared header navigation across all pages
- Multi-column responsive footer with:
  - Conservation links
  - Get Involved section
  - About the Trust links
  - Contact details and social media icons
  - Newsletter subscription form
- Responsive CSS using Flexbox and CSS Grid
- CSS Variables for consistent colour theming
- Logo integration in the site header
- Mobile-friendly breakpoints for tablets and phones

### Technical
- Pure HTML5 and CSS3 (no JavaScript frameworks)
- Semantic HTML structure
- Accessible navigation with ARIA labels
- SVG social media icons (Facebook, Instagram, WhatsApp)

---

## Future Planned Updates

### Planned
- Form validation and backend integration for enquiry and contact forms
- Image optimisation and additional project photo galleries
- Dark mode / high-contrast theme option
- Blog / Conservation News section
- Multi-language support (English / isiXhosa)

